sysh (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Approvals: signed FIDO2-grade channel (§9).
    - sysh approver add/list/remove: registered approver keys in
      /etc/sysh/approvers; sk-* (hardware-backed) keys recommended,
      software keys allowed with a warning.
    - sysh approve --show / --sig: sign the exact request bytes with
      ssh-keygen -Y sign (namespace sysh-approve) and submit; SSHSIG
      verified in-process (golang.org/x/crypto/ssh) — no ssh-keygen
      dependency on the verify path. Signature bound to the request
      content, namespace, and a registered key; requests stay TTL'd
      and single-use.
  * sysh-mcp: `sy mcp` stdio MCP server (§10) for agent harnesses —
    tools sy_exec, sy_docs, sy_policy over plain SSH as the sy user;
    approval-required (exit 30) surfaced with the request id; no
    approval power of any kind in tool space.

 -- xezpeleta <xezpeleta@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

sysh (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 1: argv-policy login shell for AI agents.
    - Gateway: printable-ASCII argv split, exact-length matching, opt-in
      rest patterns, deny rules with prefix semantics, per-rule timeouts
      with process-group kill backstop, 1 MiB output cap.
    - Containment: NoNewPrivs re-exec, seccomp not yet (phase 2),
      systemd scope execution with no-scope fallback, ptrace_scope=1.
    - Events: journald records with kernel attestation (_UID, _AUDIT_
      LOGINUID), key attribution (fingerprint, key id), policy hash,
      pre/post phases; auditd integration (sysh_exec, sysh_policy,
      sysh_lockdown keys).
  * Control channel: auth add/list/remove (option allowlist, canonical
    comma-separated authorized_keys lines, fingerprint dedup), policy
    install/lint (denylist, warn-ack classes, permissive gated on
    active auditd rules), doctor (22 checks), lockdown, journal-group.
  * Packaging: systemd tmpfiles, sy user with shell-takeover refusal,
    sshd drop-in with validated rollback, audit rules with uid
    substitution, selfcheck in postinst.

 -- xezpeleta <xezpeleta@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
